    "architecture": "aarch64",
    "context": "Native pipe2 null-output errors under descriptor pressure. Root and UID/GID1000 cohorts run [1280,1280,2560,13] checks each: exact errors and pair behavior, immediate descriptor state, canaries and refill restoration, retained aliases/data/cursor/queue. Limits48/64, zero through three free slots, four ordinary flags, five upper register patterns, eight aligned/unaligned/fault/nil outputs. Baselines fail160 of10266 checks per architecture only because early nil EFAULT masks EMFILE with fewer than two slots. Corrected Vinix and actual same-ELF Linux6.12.51 pass10266. Only the early nil branch is removed; flag validation, private endpoint construction, paired slot adoption, existing checked copy and cleanup stay unchanged. Complete generated C outside checked-wrapper body/prototype is identical. No new allocation, destructor, observer or asynchronous borrow. Sixteen fixture allocas and no hidden heap/index helpers. Two warmed 200-cycle pressure cohorts exercise nil with zero/one slots, real pair transfer/alias/EOF with two slots and both cross-page and nil EFAULT with three slots, retaining exact slab/large-page storage. Four production builds, six guest cases per architecture, eight host test files, 64 frozen inventory inputs, unchanged allocation allowance failures, source/C/ELF identity and empty complete preflight drift, active assertion/passing-baseline negative controls and independent refusal-lifetime review are bound. GNU/translated/ELF32, legacy x86 pipe, constructor/growth budget injection, table growth, concurrent limit/close and copy-before-publication/output-copy rollback races remain separate. No new desktop performance qualification or broad section15 completion is claimed.",
